        "original_id": "6a8cbb30-c118-59b0-a326-0cbfc885353b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Augusta Canal, Savannah River, Augusta, New Orleans\n- Systems: New Orleans Outfall Canals, levees, floodwalls\n- Infrastructure: Butt Memorial Bridge, 15th Street\n\nFacts:\n- The Augusta Canal is fed by the Savannah River.\n- The Augusta Canal passes through three levels across approximately 13 miles in suburban and urban Augusta before its water returns to the river at various locations.\n- The New Orleans Outfall Canals have 13 miles of levees and floodwalls lining their sides.\n- The Butt Memorial Bridge is a road bridge in Augusta, Georgia that carries 15th Street over the Augusta Canal.",
